  "id": "active-memory",
  "term": "active memory",
  "definition": "Active memory is the ability to bring to mind, without prompting, the relevant facts of a matter, keep them in mind long enough to grasp how they relate to one another, and form a rational judgment about them. In this historical source, the term is used in discussing mental capacity for making a will.",
